.TH HOWDY 1

.SH NAME
howdy \- Windows Hello™ style facial authentication for Linux

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B howdy
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
\fIcommand\fR
[\fIarguments\fR]

.SH DESCRIPTION
Howdy provides Windows Hello™ style authentication for Linux. Use your built-in IR emitters and camera in combination with facial recognition to prove who you are.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-U, \-\-user \fIUSER\fR
Run as a different user, requires sudo.
.TP
.B \-y, \-\-yes
Answer yes to every question.
.TP
.B \-C, \-\-config \fIPATH\fR
Path to the config file (default: /etc/howdy/howdy.ini).
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the current version number.

.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B add [\fIUSER\fR] [\fILABEL\fR]
Add a new face model for a user.
.TP
.B clear [\fIUSER\fR]
Remove all face models for a user.
.TP
.B config
Open the config file in your default editor.
.TP
.B disable \fIon\fR|\fBoff\fR
Disable or enable howdy.
.TP
.B list [\fIUSER\fR]
List all saved face models for a user.
.TP
.B remove \fIUSER\fR \fIID\fR
Remove a specific model for a user.
.TP
.B snapshot [\fIPATH\fR]
Take a snapshot of your camera input.
.TP
.B test [\fIUSER\fR]
Test the camera and recognition methods.
.TP
.B check [\fIUSER\fR] [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
Check if the current user is recognized (for scripts).
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-timeout \fISECONDS\fR
Timeout in seconds for the check (default: 10).
.TP
.B \-\-quiet
Run in quiet mode with no output.
.RE

.SH EXIT CODES
.TP
.B 0
Success - user recognized or command completed successfully.
.TP
.B 1
Failure - user not recognized, authentication failed, or error occurred.
.TP
.B 124
Timeout occurred during recognition check.

.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Add a face model for the current user:
.B howdy add
.TP
.B howdy add john "My laptop"
.TP
.TP
Test the camera:
.B howdy test
.TP
.TP
Check if current user is recognized (for scripts):
.B howdy check
.B howdy check --quiet --timeout 5
.TP
.TP
List all saved models:
.B howdy list
.TP
.TP
Remove model #1 for user john:
.B howdy remove john 1

.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B HOME
Used to determine the user's home directory.
.TP
.B USER
Current username.

.SH FILES
.TP
.B /etc/howdy/howdy.ini
Howdy configuration file.
.TP
.B ~/.howdy/models/
Directory containing face models for the user.
.TP
.B /var/log/auth.log
Authentication logs.

